---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/aspe/aspe1521.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — the Statement of Financial Position, Named \"Balance Sheet\"" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. Minimum Line Items" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Classified vs Unclassified Presentation" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Assets" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. Liabilities" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Owners' Equity Components" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Retractable or Mandatorily Redeemable Shares — a Distinctive Presentation Item" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — a Classified Balance Sheet Structure" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Worked Example — Presenting Retractable Shares Charged to Retained Earnings" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Relationship to IAS 1's Statement of Financial Position" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s16", label: "16. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
</div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">A snapshot of financial position, under a deliberately retained older name</div><div class="principle">ASPE Section 1521 sets OUT the MINIMUM content and PRESENTATION requirements FOR the BALANCE Sheet — the STATEMENT presenting an ENTERPRISE'S assets, LIABILITIES, and OWNERS' equity AS of a SPECIFIC date. NOTABLY, ASPE RETAINS the TRADITIONAL "BALANCE Sheet" terminology THROUGHOUT, RATHER than the "STATEMENT of Financial POSITION" naming CONVENTION IFRS adopted, REFLECTING ASPE'S broader ROOTS in PRE-2011 Canadian GAAP TERMINOLOGY (see the COMPANION terminology DISCUSSION at the START of this LIBRARY'S ASPE series).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Statement of Financial Position, Named "Balance Sheet"</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">One of the four required primary statements</div><div class="principle">This Section applies to the PRESENTATION of the BALANCE Sheet — ONE of the FOUR required PRIMARY statements COMPRISING a COMPLETE set of ASPE financial STATEMENTS, PRESENTING an ENTERPRISE'S financial POSITION at a SPECIFIC point in TIME.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>Minimum Line Items</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">The essential categories a Balance Sheet must present</div><div class="check-list"><span>Cash, accounts receivable, inventories, investments</span><span>Property, plant, and equipment; intangible assets; goodwill</span><span>Accounts payable, current portion of long-term debt, long-term debt</span><span>Share capital, retained earnings, and other owners' equity components</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Classified vs Unclassified Presentation</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Current/non-current split, or an alternative liquidity-based order</div><div class="text-supporting">MOST ASPE preparers USE a CLASSIFIED Balance SHEET — distinguishing CURRENT from NON-current assets and LIABILITIES per SECTION 1510 (see the COMPANION poster) — THOUGH an UNCLASSIFIED, liquidity-ORDERED presentation MAY instead be USED where it PROVIDES more RELIABLE and RELEVANT information (TYPICALLY relevant FOR certain FINANCIAL institutions or OTHER specialized ENTERPRISES).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Assets</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Current and non-current categories, per their governing Sections</div><div class="text-supporting">ASSETS are PRESENTED according TO their SPECIFIC governing ASPE Section — INVENTORIES per SECTION 3031, INVESTMENTS per SECTION 3051, PROPERTY, plant, AND equipment per SECTION 3061, GOODWILL and INTANGIBLE assets per SECTION 3064 — WITH the CURRENT/non-current DISTINCTION from Section 1510 APPLIED throughout.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>Liabilities</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Current and long-term obligations, clearly distinguished</div><div class="text-supporting">LIABILITIES are PRESENTED distinguishing CURRENT from LONG-term obligations, WITH the CURRENT portion of LONG-term debt PRESENTED separately WITHIN current LIABILITIES — REFLECTING the CALLABLE debt and OTHER classification RULES discussed in Section 1510.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Owners' Equity Components</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Share capital, contributed surplus, and retained earnings</div><div class="text-supporting">OWNERS' equity COMPRISES share CAPITAL, contributed SURPLUS or OTHER reserves, and RETAINED earnings — SIGNIFICANTLY simpler THAN the EQUIVALENT IFRS equity SECTION, GIVEN ASPE'S absence OF any accumulated OTHER comprehensive INCOME reserve (see the COMPANION Section 1520 poster).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Retractable or Mandatorily Redeemable Shares — a Distinctive Presentation Item</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A recurring feature of Canadian private-company tax planning arrangements</div><div class="text-supporting">A GENUINELY distinctive Balance SHEET presentation issue ARISES with RETRACTABLE or MANDATORILY redeemable SHARES issued in a TAX planning ARRANGEMENT — COMMON in Canadian PRIVATE company STRUCTURES. WHERE the EFFECT of CLASSIFYING such SHARES as a FINANCIAL liability is CHARGED to RETAINED earnings, an ENTERPRISE must DISCLOSE, on the FACE of the BALANCE Sheet, the AMOUNT charged TO retained EARNINGS for ALL classes of SUCH shares — a SPECIFIC, EXPLICIT face-of-STATEMENT disclosure REQUIREMENT reflecting a GENUINELY common Canadian PRIVATE-enterprise fact PATTERN (see SECTION 3856 for the FULL financial INSTRUMENTS treatment).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — a Classified Balance Sheet Structure</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The conventional current/non-current split</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A manufacturing company's Balance Sheet</div><div class="wk-body">A private manufacturer presents current assets of $4,200,000, non-current assets of $9,800,000, current liabilities of $2,100,000, long-term debt of $5,000,000, and owners' equity of $6,900,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">TOTAL assets ($4,200,000 + $9,800,000 = $14,000,000) EQUAL total LIABILITIES and OWNERS' equity ($2,100,000 + $5,000,000 + $6,900,000 = <strong>$14,000,000</strong>), PRESENTED in the CONVENTIONAL classified BALANCE Sheet FORMAT.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Worked Example — Presenting Retractable Shares Charged to Retained Earnings</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">The explicit face-of-statement disclosure this Section requires</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A family business's tax-planning share structure</div><div class="wk-body">A private company has retractable preferred shares issued as part of a tax planning arrangement, classified as a financial liability under Section 3856, with $180,000 of the reclassification effect charged to retained earnings.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY discloses, ON the FACE of the BALANCE Sheet, the $180,000 AMOUNT charged TO retained EARNINGS for THIS class of SHARES — a SPECIFIC, EXPLICIT disclosure this SECTION requires BEYOND the GENERAL retained EARNINGS presentation.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What Section 1521 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>All minimum line items, classified as current/non-current where a classified presentation is used</span><span>Owners' equity components, including share capital and retained earnings</span><span>Amount charged to retained earnings for retractable or mandatorily redeemable shares in a tax planning arrangement, on the face of the Balance Sheet</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgment matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Whether a classified or unclassified presentation better serves users, given the enterprise's specific circumstances</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Generally minimal — this Section is primarily a presentation standard, with measurement governed by the underlying asset/liability-specific Sections</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 1's Statement of Financial Position</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASPE Section 1521 vs IAS 1</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASPE Section 1521</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 1</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Statement name</span><span>"Balance Sheet"</span><span>"Statement of Financial Position"</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Classified vs unclassified choice</span><span>Available</span><span>Available — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">BROADLY converged IN structure, WITH the PERSISTENT "BALANCE Sheet" terminology BEING the MOST visible SURFACE-level divergence FROM current IFRS naming CONVENTIONS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where this Section's requirements apply</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Concept</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Overall Balance Sheet structure</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span></span><span>Governs presentation of all asset, liability, and equity line items</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 1510</span><span>Current Assets and Current Liabilities — supplies the current/non-current classification this Section's classified presentation applies</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Section 3856</span><span>Financial Instruments — governs the retractable/mandatorily redeemable share classification this Section requires disclosure of</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s16"><span class="num">16</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Retractable or mandatorily redeemable shares (RoMRS)</div><div class="glossary-def">Shares issued in a tax planning arrangement, classified as a financial liability under Section 3856, requiring specific face-of-Balance-Sheet disclosure of any amount charged to retained earnings.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Classified Balance Sheet</div><div class="glossary-def">A Balance Sheet presentation distinguishing current from non-current assets and liabilities.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (ASPE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge is">IS</span> Income Statement </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge sre">SRE</span> Statement of Retained Earnings / Statement of Changes in Equity </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge scf">SCF</span> Cash Flow Statement</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.aspe1521 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
